  {
   "id": "loop_vcs",
   "title": "Verifying loops with invariants and variants",
   "prompt": "<p>Extend the weakest-precondition calculator to annotated loops <code>[\"while\", c, inv, variant, body]</code>: <code>inv</code> is the loop invariant and <code>variant</code> an integer expression that must decrease (or <code>None</code> to prove only partial correctness). The starter has the previous problem's helpers and a correct <code>sub</code>.</p>\n<p><code>vcs(prog, Q)</code> returns <code>(W, conditions)</code>, where <code>W</code> is the precondition and <code>conditions</code> is a list of <code>(kind, formula)</code> pairs, each of which must be valid. For a loop with postcondition <em>Q</em> (the wp of what follows it), the loop's precondition is <em>I</em>, and it adds, in this order:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>(\"preserve\", I ∧ c ⇒ wp(body, I))</code>;</li>\n<li><code>(\"exit\", I ∧ ¬c ⇒ Q)</code>;</li>\n<li>if there is a variant <em>V</em>: <code>(\"bounded\", I ∧ c ⇒ 0 ≤ V)</code> and <code>(\"decreases\", I ∧ c ⇒ wp(body, V &lt; v0)[v0 := V])</code>, where <code>v0</code> is the variable name <code>\"_v0\"</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Conditions from loops inside a loop's body or inside an <code>if</code> come out too (in any order). Then <code>verify(P, prog, Q, lo=-6, hi=6)</code> returns a list of <code>(kind, counterexample)</code> for every condition that fails, with <code>(\"entry\", P ⇒ W)</code> checked first; an empty list means the program is verified (within the range).</p>",
   "starter": "import itertools\n\nOPS = {\"+\": lambda a, b: a + b, \"-\": lambda a, b: a - b, \"*\": lambda a, b: a * b,\n       \"<\": lambda a, b: a < b, \"<=\": lambda a, b: a <= b, \"==\": lambda a, b: a == b,\n       \"!=\": lambda a, b: a != b, \"and\": lambda a, b: a and b, \"or\": lambda a, b: a or b,\n       \"=>\": lambda a, b: (not a) or b}\n\ndef ev(e, env):\n    match e:\n        case bool() | int():\n            return e\n        case str():\n            return env[e]\n        case [\"not\", a]:\n            return not ev(a, env)\n        case [op, a, b]:\n            return OPS[op](ev(a, env), ev(b, env))\n    raise ValueError(f\"bad expression {e!r}\")\n\ndef variables(e):\n    match e:\n        case str():\n            return {e}\n        case bool() | int():\n            return set()\n        case [_, *args]:\n            return set().union(*map(variables, args))\n\ndef counterexample(e, lo=-6, hi=6):\n    \"\"\"Values in lo..hi for the variables of e that make e false, or None (from the notes).\"\"\"\n    names = sorted(variables(e))\n    for values in itertools.product(range(lo, hi + 1), repeat=len(names)):\n        env = dict(zip(names, values))\n        if not ev(e, env):\n            return env\n    return None\n\n\ndef sub(e, x, r):\n    match e:\n        case str() if e == x:\n            return r\n        case bool() | int() | str():\n            return e\n        case [op, *args]:\n            return [op] + [sub(a, x, r) for a in args]\n\ndef vcs(prog, Q):\n    pass\n\ndef verify(P, prog, Q, lo=-6, hi=6):\n    pass\n",
   "hint": "<p>Make <code>vcs</code> collect conditions into a list it passes along: a helper <code>go(prog, Q, out)</code> that works backwards like <code>wp</code>, and for a loop calls <code>go(body, inv, out)</code> to get wp(body, <em>I</em>). For the variant, compute <code>go(body, [\"&lt;\", V, \"_v0\"], out)</code>, then substitute <code>V</code> for <code>\"_v0\"</code>. (That second call collects the inner loops' conditions again; duplicates do no harm.)</p>",
   "solution": "import itertools\n\nOPS = {\"+\": lambda a, b: a + b, \"-\": lambda a, b: a - b, \"*\": lambda a, b: a * b,\n       \"<\": lambda a, b: a < b, \"<=\": lambda a, b: a <= b, \"==\": lambda a, b: a == b,\n       \"!=\": lambda a, b: a != b, \"and\": lambda a, b: a and b, \"or\": lambda a, b: a or b,\n       \"=>\": lambda a, b: (not a) or b}\n\ndef ev(e, env):\n    match e:\n        case bool() | int():\n            return e\n        case str():\n            return env[e]\n        case [\"not\", a]:\n            return not ev(a, env)\n        case [op, a, b]:\n            return OPS[op](ev(a, env), ev(b, env))\n    raise ValueError(f\"bad expression {e!r}\")\n\ndef variables(e):\n    match e:\n        case str():\n            return {e}\n        case bool() | int():\n            return set()\n        case [_, *args]:\n            return set().union(*map(variables, args))\n\ndef counterexample(e, lo=-6, hi=6):\n    \"\"\"Values in lo..hi for the variables of e that make e false, or None (from the notes).\"\"\"\n    names = sorted(variables(e))\n    for values in itertools.product(range(lo, hi + 1), repeat=len(names)):\n        env = dict(zip(names, values))\n        if not ev(e, env):\n            return env\n    return None\n\n\ndef sub(e, x, r):\n    match e:\n        case str() if e == x:\n            return r\n        case bool() | int() | str():\n            return e\n        case [op, *args]:\n            return [op] + [sub(a, x, r) for a in args]\n\ndef _go(prog, Q, out):\n    for s in reversed(prog):\n        match s:\n            case [\"set\", x, e]:\n                Q = sub(Q, x, e)\n            case [\"if\", c, then, other]:\n                Q = [\"and\", [\"=>\", c, _go(then, Q, out)], [\"=>\", [\"not\", c], _go(other, Q, out)]]\n            case [\"assert\", c]:\n                Q = [\"and\", c, Q]\n            case [\"while\", c, inv, var, body]:\n                out.append((\"preserve\", [\"=>\", [\"and\", inv, c], _go(body, inv, out)]))\n                out.append((\"exit\", [\"=>\", [\"and\", inv, [\"not\", c]], Q]))\n                if var is not None:\n                    out.append((\"bounded\", [\"=>\", [\"and\", inv, c], [\"<=\", 0, var]]))\n                    dec = _go(body, [\"<\", var, \"_v0\"], [])\n                    out.append((\"decreases\", [\"=>\", [\"and\", inv, c], sub(dec, \"_v0\", var)]))\n                Q = inv\n    return Q\n\ndef vcs(prog, Q):\n    out = []\n    W = _go(prog, Q, out)\n    return W, out\n\ndef verify(P, prog, Q, lo=-6, hi=6):\n    W, conds = vcs(prog, Q)\n    failed = []\n    for kind, f in [(\"entry\", [\"=>\", P, W])] + conds:\n        c = counterexample(f, lo, hi)\n        if c is not None:\n            failed.append((kind, c))\n    return failed\n",
   "tests": [
    {
     "label": "Division by repeated subtraction",
     "type": "assert",
     "code": "def div(inv, var):\n    return [[\"set\", \"q\", 0], [\"set\", \"r\", \"x\"],\n            [\"while\", [\"<=\", \"y\", \"r\"], inv, var, [[\"set\", \"r\", [\"-\", \"r\", \"y\"]], [\"set\", \"q\", [\"+\", \"q\", 1]]]]]\npre = [\"and\", [\"<=\", 0, \"x\"], [\"<\", 0, \"y\"]]\npost = [\"and\", [\"==\", \"x\", [\"+\", [\"*\", \"q\", \"y\"], \"r\"]], [\"and\", [\"<=\", 0, \"r\"], [\"<\", \"r\", \"y\"]]]\ninv = [\"and\", [\"==\", \"x\", [\"+\", [\"*\", \"q\", \"y\"], \"r\"]], [\"<=\", 0, \"r\"]]\ninv_y = [\"and\", inv, [\"<\", 0, \"y\"]]\nassert verify(pre, div(inv, None), post, -3, 3) == []\nassert verify(pre, div(inv_y, \"r\"), post, -3, 3) == []\nkinds = [k for k, c in verify(pre, div(inv, \"r\"), post, -3, 3)]\nassert kinds == [\"decreases\"], kinds\nW, conds = vcs(div(inv_y, \"r\"), post)\nassert [k for k, f in conds] == [\"preserve\", \"exit\", \"bounded\", \"decreases\"]\n"
    },
    {
     "label": "Invariants that are too weak or wrong",
     "type": "assert",
     "code": "def div(inv):\n    return [[\"set\", \"q\", 0], [\"set\", \"r\", \"x\"],\n            [\"while\", [\"<=\", \"y\", \"r\"], inv, None, [[\"set\", \"r\", [\"-\", \"r\", \"y\"]], [\"set\", \"q\", [\"+\", \"q\", 1]]]]]\npre = [\"and\", [\"<=\", 0, \"x\"], [\"<\", 0, \"y\"]]\npost = [\"and\", [\"==\", \"x\", [\"+\", [\"*\", \"q\", \"y\"], \"r\"]], [\"and\", [\"<=\", 0, \"r\"], [\"<\", \"r\", \"y\"]]]\nweak = [\"==\", \"x\", [\"+\", [\"*\", \"q\", \"y\"], \"r\"]]\nr = verify(pre, div(weak), post, -3, 3)\nassert [k for k, c in r] == [\"exit\"], r\nc = r[0][1]\nassert c[\"x\"] == c[\"q\"] * c[\"y\"] + c[\"r\"] and c[\"r\"] < c[\"y\"] and c[\"r\"] < 0, c\nwrong = [\"==\", \"q\", 0]\nassert {k for k, c in verify(pre, div(wrong), post, -3, 3)} == {\"preserve\", \"exit\"}\n"
    },
    {
     "label": "Summing 0 + 1 + ... + (n - 1)",
     "type": "assert",
     "code": "prog = [[\"set\", \"i\", 0], [\"set\", \"s\", 0],\n        [\"while\", [\"<\", \"i\", \"n\"],\n         [\"and\", [\"==\", [\"*\", 2, \"s\"], [\"*\", \"i\", [\"-\", \"i\", 1]]], [\"<=\", \"i\", \"n\"]],\n         [\"-\", \"n\", \"i\"],\n         [[\"set\", \"s\", [\"+\", \"s\", \"i\"]], [\"set\", \"i\", [\"+\", \"i\", 1]]]]]\npost = [\"==\", [\"*\", 2, \"s\"], [\"*\", \"n\", [\"-\", \"n\", 1]]]\nassert verify([\"<=\", 0, \"n\"], prog, post) == []\nassert [k for k, c in verify(True, prog, post)] == [\"entry\"]\n"
    },
    {
     "label": "Nested loops: multiplication by repeated increment",
     "type": "assert",
     "hidden": true,
     "code": "inner = [\"while\", [\"<\", \"j\", \"b\"], [\"and\", [\"==\", \"p\", [\"+\", [\"*\", \"i\", \"b\"], \"j\"]], [\"and\", [\"<=\", \"j\", \"b\"], [\"and\", [\"<\", \"i\", \"a\"], [\"<=\", 0, \"b\"]]]], [\"-\", \"b\", \"j\"],\n         [[\"set\", \"p\", [\"+\", \"p\", 1]], [\"set\", \"j\", [\"+\", \"j\", 1]]]]\nouter = [\"while\", [\"<\", \"i\", \"a\"], [\"and\", [\"==\", \"p\", [\"*\", \"i\", \"b\"]], [\"and\", [\"<=\", \"i\", \"a\"], [\"<=\", 0, \"b\"]]], [\"-\", \"a\", \"i\"],\n         [[\"set\", \"j\", 0], inner, [\"set\", \"i\", [\"+\", \"i\", 1]]]]\nprog = [[\"set\", \"p\", 0], [\"set\", \"i\", 0], outer]\npre = [\"and\", [\"<=\", 0, \"a\"], [\"<=\", 0, \"b\"]]\nassert verify(pre, prog, [\"==\", \"p\", [\"*\", \"a\", \"b\"]], -2, 2) == []\nbad_inner = inner[:2] + [[\"and\", [\"==\", \"p\", [\"+\", [\"*\", \"i\", \"b\"], \"j\"]], [\"<=\", \"j\", \"b\"]]] + inner[3:]\nbad = [[\"set\", \"p\", 0], [\"set\", \"i\", 0], outer[:4] + [[[\"set\", \"j\", 0], bad_inner, [\"set\", \"i\", [\"+\", \"i\", 1]]]]]\nassert verify(pre, bad, [\"==\", \"p\", [\"*\", \"a\", \"b\"]], -2, 2) != []\n"
    }
   ]
  }
